  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nCustom Elements will sometimes need to declare that they are focus-able.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nThere are several solutions to do this today:\n\n- The element can delegate to an element within the shadowDOM, e.g. `shadowRoot.innerHTML = '<div tabindex=0>'`. However this creates a potentially unnecessary additional DOM node.\n- The element can sprout a `tabindex` attribute on `connectedCallback` - e.g. `connectedCallback() { this.setAttribute('tabindex', '0'); }`. However this means it is sprouting attributes, which can trigger document mutation observers (IOW it affects performance), and can potentially conflict with already set attributes or attributes set later on (IOW racey).\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nI think providing `ElementInternals.prototype.tabIndex` as a setter which can act like `ElementInternals.prototype.role` - where setting it to a value will indicate that this element should use this value, if the `tabindex=` attribute is not provided. \n\n```webidl\npartial interface ElementInternals {\n  [CEReactions] attribute long tabIndex;\n}\n```\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
